for mode,v in ctl['continuous'].items():
 for outcome in ('raw_operating_contrast','inventory_adjusted_contrast'):contrast('Continuous SOC',outcome.replace('_contrast',''),mode,v[outcome]['all299'])
tab('Table S6. Complete private-cost condition matrix.',['Family','Setting','Question','Paired days','Δ (cents/day)','95% interval','Benefiting HH (%)'],rows,'DFL minus its condition-matched MSE comparator, seed 11. Frozen repricing changes no action; frozen reoptimization changes the controller objective; matched retraining changes the signal under that objective. Macro estimands and held-out/known cohorts are separately retained in control_transfer_summary. Inventory-adjusted cost is not actual retail settlement.')
p('Continuous SOC uses daily 24-hour QPs and two-day training rollout. Of the original sampled anchors, 4,088 training and 1,021 validation windows have the next day in the appropriate split. Each training window starts at 5 kWh; test carries energy across 328 complete evaluated household segments and does not reset every two days. The terminal inventory function includes both linear and quadratic terms. Segment corrections telescope as V(start)−V(end); invalid observation boundaries are common across arms. Average daily terminal energy is about 5.22 kWh for matched learners. The finite-difference gradient check includes 20 real examples, three joint net/SOC directions and three step scales, with a maximum best-scale absolute discrepancy of 5.32×10⁻¹⁰. This establishes local KKT consistency, not a globally smooth active-set map.')
