tab('Table S9. Matched 27-household geographic-cohort check.',['Outcome','Grouped gap','Dispersed gap','Difference of gaps','95% interval'],rows,'Gap is DFL minus continued MSE. Same 27 locations and 160 dates, same known/held-out role counts. Matching uses pretest log daily gross demand and PV capacity; standardized differences are approximately −0.029 and −0.011. The dispersed cohort spans 21 postcodes with no more than two households per postcode. Units follow outcome names: AUD/owner-day, percentage points, kW or kWh/day. No real-neighborhood connectivity or causal geographic effect is inferred.')
p('The main nine deployment cells retain three-seed paired household-level cost and voltage summaries. Among full ToU owners, 3.6–7.3% have higher mean cost across fixed-panel/adoption combinations. In the 28-owner case, nonowner exposure changes are −0.3479/−0.2793/−0.2725 percentage points across the three fixed panels, versus −0.5317/−0.5103/−0.4881 for owners. Both groups can benefit on average while individual sites or customers still lose. Capacity and pretest-demand tertile cutpoints are fixed from known pretest records, not selected for subgroup significance; the full results remain descriptive without additional subgroup significance claims.')
