p('All 20 StoreNet power CSV files were downloaded and inspected. Verified PV household IDs are 1,2,3,4,5,7,10,11,13,17. There are 3,439 complete target days before the seven-day-history requirement and 2,224 scored days after it. Mean nominal capacity is not inferred from production maxima. Original minute-grid power missingness is retained; the companion interpolated energy pipeline is unused. Public OPSD household data were also assessed, but cumulative-meter interpretation, load reconstruction and insufficient verified capacity fields made them a weaker frozen-transfer candidate; its download and screening record is retained without claiming an external result from that dataset.')
h('S11. Numerical and independent consistency checks')
p('Original strictly convex battery-layer checks include primal state and energy balance, KKT differentiation, action selection under alternative regularization, independent settlement, and an equal-buy/sell negative control. The final revision adds independent measured-cost recomputation on expanded dispatch, a real-data continuous-SOC gradient audit, inventory-boundary reconciliation and per-element export-curtailment/lost-revenue verification. AC local sensitivities are checked against full nonlinear replay and halved perturbations. These checks distinguish model implementation from field fidelity; no solver residual is treated as evidence about unknown household wiring, impedances, phase assignments, or inverter response.')
standard=read('results/revision_dispatch_audit.json');external=read('results/storenet_external_postrun_audit.json');settlement=read('research/independent_settlement_verification.json');ac=read('network_revision_audit.json')
assert standard['status']==external['status']==ac['status']=='PASS'
assert not settlement['failures'] and not settlement['not_ready'] and all(x['passed'] for x in settlement['checks'])
p(f"State and settlement checks passed for all {standard['n_completed_artifacts']} completed Ausgrid revision dispatch files and {len(external['checked_dispatch_files'])} external dispatch files. External recomputation had zero stored-cost discrepancy; the largest rounded-state bound and cyclic-end discrepancies were {external['max_storage_rounded_soc_bound_violation_kwh']:.2e} and {external['max_storage_rounded_cyclic_end_error_kwh']:.2e} kWh. An additional independent settlement implementation recomputed all {len(settlement['checks'])} expanded comparison files directly from observed load, generation and saved charge/discharge actions, with no failed or unfinished file in that comparison.")
p(f"The network revision contains {ac['new_scenarios']} completed scenario results: {ac['newly_executed_ac_replays']} new nonlinear AC replays and {ac['reused_original_geo_replays_with_new_common_mask']} original geographic replays restricted to the new common-date mask. All new replays converged, and the maximum absolute active-power balance residual was {ac['maximum_balance_residual_kw']:.2e} kW. Numerical convergence does not imply satisfaction of voltage or equipment constraints. Export checks include curtailed generation and foregone export revenue.")
p('The local reproduction package contains source-data acquisition records, model weights, derived inputs, saved dispatch, numerical audits and the code required to reconstruct the reported tables and figures. It supports independent cost, observation-mask and checkpoint checks. Fresh training from source data additionally requires the documented public-data acquisition and cache-generation steps. Source-data and software licenses are recorded with the corresponding materials; the package is a local research artifact and has not been assigned a public DOI.')
